# Security (Lane A, Oct 2026): this project has no "public" output directory, so by default
# Vercel statically serves every git-tracked file in the repo at its own path - including
# internal docs, SQL schema, and dev tooling that was never meant to be a public page/asset.
# Everything listed here is confirmed NOT read by any api/** function or by the build: api/**
# functions bundle their lib/** and js/** imports at build time (nothing below is in that
# import graph), and GitHub Actions runs scripts/**, ops/** and .github/workflows/** from its
# own `actions/checkout` clone of the git repo, never through this deployment.
#
# lib/** and js/** are deliberately NOT listed here: lib/** is a build import for api/**, and
# js/** is real client-side script served to every browser. Their own static-source exposure
# (lib/**) is a separate, larger architecture fix (moving to a dedicated public/ root) - tracked
# as Step 3, not fixed by this file.

CLAUDE.md
_pd.mjs

# ROOT-ANCHORED (Oct 2026, THE actual cause of the lib/ops/depthProbe.js outage below): every one
# of these previously had no leading slash, which in gitignore/.vercelignore syntax means "a
# directory with this name at ANY depth", not just the repo root - confirmed live and reproduced
# with git check-ignore: the unanchored "ops/" pattern matched BOTH the intended root-level ops/
# (dev tooling) AND lib/ops/ (depthProbe.js, fillLadder.js, backtestCore.js - all three real
# runtime imports of api/usageDashboard.js). That silently deleted lib/ops/ from every deploy
# bundle the moment this file's first version shipped, and because the broken import is a
# top-level `import` in api/usageDashboard.js (not a dynamic one), EVERY request to that
# function failed with FUNCTION_INVOCATION_FAILED / ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND, not just the ops tasks
# this file's second version (scripts/** exceptions) was written to fix - that fix was real but
# masked by this bigger, earlier break. A leading slash anchors each pattern to the repo root,
# exactly like the already-correct "scripts/**" entry below (which is unambiguous only because it
# has no bare, unanchored sibling elsewhere in the tree - verified no second scripts/ directory
# exists under lib/ or elsewhere; only ops/ had a same-named collision, under lib/ops/).
/docs/
/ops/
/test/
/smoke-artifacts/
/.github/

# scripts/** is dev/ops tooling only, with exceptions for files api/usageDashboard.js itself
# reads at request time: warm-list.json via vercel.json's own includeFiles, plus FOUR files it
# dynamically `import()`s at runtime for ops tasks (confirmed live, Oct 2026 - this file's first
# version excluded all of scripts/** on the stated assumption that "api/** functions bundle
# their lib/** and js/** imports at build time (nothing below is in that import graph)", which is
# true for STATIC imports but not for these - a dynamic import() is invisible to that build-time
# bundling and was silently broken in production, surfacing as FUNCTION_INVOCATION_FAILED on
# every task=enginecheck/buildcanonical/buildvinindex/buildspecmarketcache call the moment this
# file's first version deployed). Keep all four reachable; everything else in scripts/** is true
# dev/ops tooling run only via GitHub Actions, never imported by a deployed function.
scripts/**
!scripts/warm-list.json
!scripts/crossProductCheck.js
!scripts/buildCanonical.js
!scripts/buildVinIndex.js
!scripts/buildSpecMarketCache.js

# .env.example and .gitignore are not read by the Vercel build in any way (safe to drop from
# the upload entirely). package.json/package-lock.json/vercel.json are NOT listed here even
# though they already 404 live - Vercel's build itself needs them (dependency install, function
# config, rewrites/crons); .vercelignore would strip them from the upload and break the build,
# not just the HTTP route.
.env.example
.gitignore
